Z||000000||GodSend||03-27-2001||08:11 PM||||  Does anyone know of a good tutorial or have any advice for someone who is looking at doing some pleather/vinal work.  Square pieces are easy enough, but I am sure on how to do curvey pieces (such as a dash) with a single piece of vinal (dont want and seams)<P>thanks guys<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fyerstarter||03-27-2001||10:40 PM||||You can get vinyl to stretch to some degree by heating it with a blow dryer. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-28-2001||06:14 PM||||around corners you slit the material where it wraps around the back of the part, like a sunburst pattern but dont cut it clear to the edge. pull each piece and glue or staple it overlaping the previous one if necessary. Try experimenting on something first and youll see how I mean. Use contact cement-not spray can stuff- it wont hold I promice you! You brush it on the part and back of fabric and let it dry almost completely then stick it. after a little practice, its ez. thats the way pros do it without sewn seams. Hair dryer may help to stretch harder spots. if your covering your stock dash, sorry to say you may have to make a seam or two, it has lots of hollow and compound curves.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
